CORE
main.ii
--winx64
^\[main\.assertion\.1\] line \d+ virtual base members: SUCCESS$
^\[main\.assertion\.2\] line \d+ virtual base aligned: SUCCESS$
^\[main\.assertion\.3\] line \d+ non-virtual base: SUCCESS$
^\[main\.assertion\.4\] line \d+ base subobject aligned: SUCCESS$
^\[main\.assertion\.5\] line \d+ WRONG \(must FAIL\): FAILURE$
^VERIFICATION FAILED$
^EXIT=10$
^SIGNAL=0$
--
^warning: ignoring
^CONVERSION ERROR$
--
The Visual Studio layout re-aligned each member flattened in from a base
class, putting padding inside the base subobject, while the subobject
(and a virtual base's offset in the virtual table) started unaligned:
writes through the base went to the wrong bytes.
